#!/bin/sh
# Godzilla XS-86000 library, state, and menu foundation

# Godzilla XS-86000 is the visible identity of =sanctuary-sx=.  The technical
# identifier remains =sanctuary-sx= for containers, guest homes, manifests,
# helpers, and Xephyr display wiring.

# Shared media lives in =~/RetroPie= and is treated as a durable media library,
# not a RetroPie OS installation.  Emulator configuration, Wine prefixes, saves,
# caches, shader cache, Lutris state, and generated thumbnails stay in
# =XDG_DATA_HOME/godzilla-xs= and =XDG_CONFIG_HOME/godzilla-xs= inside the
# sanctuary guest home.

# Bus policy:
# - X68 BUS: XEiJ primary; XM6 under Wine fallback only.
# - DRIVE A: PC-98: NP2Kai primary; T98-Next under Wine fallback only.
# - DRIVE B: PC-88: QUASI88 primary; MAME fallback only, not the front end.
# - FM TOWNS: Tsugaru primary; ScummVM supplement; UNZ under Wine fallback only.
# - ARCADE BUS: MAME only.  Neo Geo is SNK Neo Geo MVS arcade hardware.
# - PC COMPATIBILITY BOARD: Wine/Lutris Japanese and period PC software.

# No Saturn bus, no Nintendo/Super Famicom bus, no FBNeo/FinalBurn Alpha arcade
# runtime, and no private/adult quarantine category.


# [[file:../../../sanctuary-sx.org::*Godzilla XS-86000 library, state, and menu foundation][Godzilla XS-86000 library, state, and menu foundation:1]]
# Initialize sanctuary-local Godzilla XS-86000 state.
set -eu

DATA_HOME="${XDG_DATA_HOME:-${HOME}/.local/share}"
CONFIG_HOME="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-${HOME}/.config}"
GODZILLA_DATA="${DATA_HOME}/godzilla-xs"
GODZILLA_CONFIG="${CONFIG_HOME}/godzilla-xs"

mkdir -p \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/xm6-typeg" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/t98-next" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/unz" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/sega-pc-9x" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/capcom-pc-9x" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/konami-pc-9x" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/jpwin9x" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/mugen" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/romlab-win32" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/mgs2-xp" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/lutris/import-plans" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/logs/winetricks" \
  "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine-tools/romlab-win32" \
  "${GODZILLA_CONFIG}/mame" \
  "${GODZILLA_CONFIG}/scummvm" \
  "${GODZILLA_CONFIG}/midi" \
  "${GODZILLA_CONFIG}/emulators"

cat > "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine/README.md" <<'WINE_README'
# Godzilla XS-86000 Wine Prefixes

Prefixes are sanctuary-local.  Do not place prefixes, caches, saves, or Lutris
runtime state in `~/RetroPie`.

- `xm6-typeg`: Win32, Windows 98. Fallback X68000 emulator route only when a
  specific user-owned title requires XM6 TypeG or XM6 Pro-68k.
- `t98-next`: Win32, Windows 98. Fallback PC-98 route only when a specific
  user-owned title requires T98-Next.
- `unz`: Win32, Windows 98. Fallback FM Towns route only when a specific
  user-owned title requires UNZ.
- `sega-pc-9x`: Win32, Windows 98 unless a title requires Windows 2000.
- `capcom-pc-9x`: Win32, Windows 98 unless a title requires Windows 2000.
- `konami-pc-9x`: Win32, Windows 98 unless a title requires Windows 2000.
- `jpwin9x`: Win32, Windows 98 general Japanese Windows 95/98 software.
- `mugen`: Win32, Windows 98/2000 per engine requirement.
- `romlab-win32`: Win32 Windows tools such as Atlas, Cartographer, WindHex32,
  YY-CHR, and Tile Molester when user-supplied.
- `mgs2-xp`: Win32, Windows XP for later material such as MGS2 Substance.

Candidate winetricks verbs are applied per executable only, with a recorded
reason and logs: corefonts, directplay, directmusic, dinput, dsound, quartz,
mfc42, mfc42u, vcrun6, vcrun2005, d3dx9.
WINE_README

cat > "${GODZILLA_DATA}/wine-tools/romlab-win32/README.md" <<'ROMLAB_README'
# Godzilla XS-86000 ROM Lab Win32 Placeholders

No Windows ROM tools are downloaded by DotCortex.  User-owned installers or
archives belong under `~/RetroPie/installers/romlab/`.

Declared future tools:

- Atlas
- Cartographer
- WindHex32
- YY-CHR
- Tile Molester

Run them from the sanctuary-local `romlab-win32` Wine prefix after the
user-owned installer/archive is supplied.
ROMLAB_README
# Godzilla XS-86000 library, state, and menu foundation:1 ends here
